        "calls": 1,
        "title": "CloudRunReader watchdog stalls silent SSE streams after 30s idle",
        "summary": "A watchdog mechanism was added to CloudRunReader in common/src/desktop-cloud/run-stream.ts to detect when an active Server-Sent Events stream stops sending data. The reader now tracks byte arrival and connection state, aborting the connection if it remains silent for 30000 ms, which is twice the server's 15-second keepalive interval. This change also introduced the CLOUD_STREAM_ID_HEADER constant to correlate logs between the server and the client, and a CloudStreamStall type to report diagnostic information about the stall when it occurs. Previously, a silent stream would remain connected until the server's 120-second cap or a 150-second request timeout expired, hiding a running turn's output from the viewer.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "operators",
        "evidence": "The diff in common/src/desktop-cloud/run-stream.ts introduces CLOUD_STREAM_IDLE_MS, the CloudStreamStall type, and a watchdog timer in CloudRunReader that aborts silent SSE connections after 30 seconds and reports the stall via an onStall callback.",
        "userVisible": false,
        "confidence": "medium",
        "unknowns": "The diff does not indicate whether the onStall callback is currently wired to any user-facing telemetry or alerting system.",
        "whyMissing": true,
